.TH WLMENU 1 2026-09-10 wlmenu "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wlmenu \- a wmenu/dmenu-style dynamic menu for Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wlmenu
.RB [ \-biPv ]
.RB [ \-f " font" ]
.RB [ \-l " lines" ]
.RB [ \-W " width" ]
.RB [ \-p " prompt" ]
.RB [ \-o " output" ]
.RB [ \-N " color" ]\c
.RB [ \-n " color" ]
.RB [ \-M " color" ]\c
.RB [ \-m " color" ]
.RB [ \-S " color" ]\c
.RB [ \-s " color" ]
.br
.B wlmenu \-\-run
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wlmenu
reads newline-separated items from standard input, filters them as the user
types, and prints the selection to standard output.  It is a Wayland-native
dmenu replacement using wlr-layer-shell; rendering is done in software
(wl_shm), so it pulls in no cairo/pango stack.
.PP
The menu starts as a single input bar (Spotlight style) and expands into a
list as soon as the query has content; clearing the query collapses it again.
Without
.B \-b
the bar is centred horizontally and floats below the top screen edge.
.PP
With an empty query,
.B Enter
cancels rather than selecting blind.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-b
Show the menu at the bottom of the screen instead of the upper centre.
.TP
.B \-i
Match case-insensitively.
.TP
.B \-l " lines"
Show at most
.I lines
item rows; the list scrolls beyond that.  Without it at most 64 rows are
shown.
.TP
.B \-W " width"
Panel width in logical pixels.  Without
.B \-W
the width is 45% of the output width, clamped to 480\-960 px, and the text size
follows it (1/32 of the width, 14\-30 px).
.TP
.B \-p " prompt"
Prompt label drawn at the left of the input bar (for example
.RB \(aq "run: " \(aq ).
.TP
.B \-P
Mask the typed input with asterisks (password mode).  Filtering still sees
the real query.
.TP
.BI \-f " font"
Font to use.  Either a path to a
.B .ttf
file, or a family description:
.RI \(dq FAMILY
.RI [ style ]
.RI [ pt | Npx ] \(dq.
A bare size is interpreted as points, as in wmenu/Pango;
.IB N px
is pixels.  Without
.B \-f
a CJK-capable system font is picked automatically.
.TP
.BI \-o " output"
Show the menu on the output with the given name (as reported by the
compositor, for example
.IR eDP-1 ).
Without it the compositor chooses the output.  An unknown name is an error.
.TP
.BI \-N " color"
Normal row background.
.TP
.BI \-n " color"
Normal row foreground.
.TP
.BI \-M " color"
Prompt/input row background.
.TP
.BI \-m " color"
Prompt/input row foreground.
.TP
.BI \-S " color"
Selected row background.
.TP
.BI \-s " color"
Selected row foreground.
.TP
.B \-\-run
Ignore stdin: list entries from
.B .desktop
files in the XDG application directories plus executables found on
.BR PATH ,
and launch the selection with
.BR "sh \-c" .
Desktop entries win when a name appears in both.  Hidden entries, entries that
need a terminal (\fBTerminal=true\fR), entries restricted to other desktops
(\fBOnlyShowIn\fR/\fBNotShowIn\fR), and non-executable files in
\fBPATH\fR directories are skipped; a localized \fBName[locale]\fR is preferred
when it matches the user's locale.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.PP
Colors are wmenu-style
.B RRGGBB
or
.B RRGGBBAA
hex values; a leading
.B #
is accepted.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Up ", " Down ", " Ctrl\-n ", " Ctrl\-p
Move the selection.
.TP
.B PgUp ", " PgDn ", " Home ", " End
Move by a page, to the first, or to the last entry.
.TP
.B Return ", " KP_Enter ", " Ctrl\-j ", " Ctrl\-m
Print the highlighted entry (or the typed query when nothing matches) and
exit.
.TP
.B Shift\-Return
Print exactly what was typed, even when something is highlighted.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Return
Print the highlighted entry and keep the menu open (repeat for multi-select).
.TP
.B Tab
Complete the highlighted entry into the input bar.
.TP
.B Escape ", " Ctrl\-c ", " Ctrl\-g
Cancel: exit without printing anything.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-h ", " Backspace
Delete the character before the caret.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-u
Clear the query.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-w
Delete the word before the caret.
.PP
Any other printable character is appended to the query.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
An entry (or the typed query) was printed, or
.B \-\-run
launched a selection.
.TP
.B 1
The menu was cancelled, stdin held no items, or an error occurred.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Wayland socket to connect to (via
.BR XDG_RUNTIME_DIR ).
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_DIRS
Searched for
.B .desktop
entries in
.B \-\-run
mode.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
The system font chain is cached here, keyed by the font directory mtimes.
.SH EXAMPLES
List files:
.PP
.EX
$ ls | wlmenu \-p \(aqopen: \(aq
.EE
.PP
Launcher bound to a key:
.PP
.EX
$ wlmenu \-\-run
.EE
.PP
Show on a specific output, case-insensitively, with width 500:
.PP
.EX
$ printf \(aqa\\nb\\n\(aq | wlmenu \-i \-o DP-1 \-W 500
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmenu (1),
.BR dmenu (1),
.BR sway (1)
